==Strategy==
By now, you should definitely have beaten [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3's moon and obtained [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]. Without him, good luck.

Do not underestimate the shy boys here, as they are magnified to extreme levels for a stage this early on in the game. Use the weak peons at the beginning of the stage to stall and stack up as many Bahamuts as you can before pushing the base. If you have any anti-red or anti-floating crowd control units, they can make this stage a lot easier. Deploying meatshields is a must here, as the shy boys will tear through everything if you don't.

You may also cheese this stage by using Li'l Wall Cat, preferably lvl 25 or higher. Once you start, immediately spam Li'l Wall. Once your cat cannon charges, use it once, then don't activate it again. If done right, you'll be able to push the doges back, and you'll be able to beat the stage without dealing with the Shy Boys (Do note that it may take a while to beat with only Li'l Wall, so its recommended to use a unit with low range but high damage, such as Kunio-kun)

